Native engine, renderer and font sources
---------------------------------------

runtime/ owns the maintained native Web engine, renderer, bridge, vendored
source dependencies, build recipe and required font inputs. Compiled native
executables, build caches and local build receipts are not source releases.
See runtime/README.md and the component LICENSE/NOTICE files for provenance
and build requirements.

Lightpanda Browser (https://github.com/lightpanda-io/browser) carries the GNU
Affero General Public License version 3 text. Its LICENSING.md declares
AGPL-3.0-only while some source/package declarations say AGPL-3.0-or-later;
both are preserved, not resolved or relicensed by this migration.
The Obscura renderer and vendored dependencies retain their own notices.
Bundled Liberation 1.07.4 fonts retain the original GPLv2 plus font-exception
notice, not a substituted modern Liberation OFL license. DejaVu and Noto
fonts retain their respective notices. Neither the root MIT license nor
Python package metadata relicenses native components or a linked executable.
Source migration is not a legal clearance for a composite binary release.

HTML named character reference data
----------------------------------

runtime/engine/src/browser/entities_data.zig retains all 2,231 entries from
web_atoms 0.3.0/entities.rs under its MIT option, including the complete notice.
The file records the locked crate hash, original data hash, upstream revision
and lossless transformation. This data extraction does not relicense native
engine code or replace the Rust HTML tokenizer's remaining internal tables.

Test fixture
------------

The string "hunter2" in mioa-headless/tests/test_axtree_observation.py is a
literal used to verify that password values are masked. It is not a
credential.

